# Derived artifacts. No data, no weights, no patient-adjacent files, ever.
#
# results/ is excluded wholesale, then exactly three aggregate artifacts per arm
# are allowed back, so the run record is inspectable without publishing anything
# image-derived:
#
#   provenance.json                  run config, hardware, commit, timestamps
#   trajectory.csv                   per-layer density and churn, by layer name
#   training_log.jsonl               per-epoch loss and timing
#   regrowth_informativeness.csv     per-layer top-k overlap between batches
#
# None of the three contains a case identifier, a file path, or any per-subject
# quantity. Everything else under results/ stays out, including:
#   - checkpoints (weights)
#   - config.yaml (embeds absolute dataset paths)
#   - console and launch logs
#   - results/diagnostics/, which is per-case and carries lesion centroids
results/**
!results/*/
!results/*/provenance.json
!results/*/trajectory.csv
!results/*/training_log.jsonl
!results/*/regrowth_informativeness.csv

# Re-excluded after the allowances above. Per-subject and image-derived: case
# IDs, lesion voxel counts and centroid coordinates. Never publishable.
results/diagnostics/

checkpoints/
*.pth
*.pt
*.ckpt

# Imaging data
*.nii
*.nii.gz
*.b2nd
*.npz
*.npy
*.mha
*.nrrd

# Notebook outputs
notebooks/**/*.ipynb_checkpoints/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

.vscode/
.idea/
